sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant A as Any instance
    participant R as cache (Redis)
    participant P as PostgreSQL

    rect rgb(235, 244, 255)
    Note over C,P: Read: GET /api/v1/books/42
    C->>A: GET /api/v1/books/42
    A->>R: MGET libra:ver:book:42 → "7"
    A->>R: GET libra:book:42:v7
    alt HIT
        R-->>A: JSON
        A-->>C: 200 · X-Cache: HIT (no DB access)
    else MISS
        R-->>A: nil
        A->>R: SET libra:book:42:v7:lock NX PX 2000 (stampede guard)
        A->>P: SELECT * FROM books WHERE id = 42
        P-->>A: row
        A->>R: SET libra:book:42:v7 JSON EX 300±10%
        A-->>C: 200 · X-Cache: MISS
    else cache down (timeout 0.3 s → circuit breaker 5 s)
        A->>P: SELECT ... (direct)
        A-->>C: 200 · X-Cache: BYPASS
    end
    end

    rect rgb(255, 243, 235)
    Note over C,P: Write: PATCH /api/v1/books/42
    C->>A: PATCH /api/v1/books/42
    A->>P: BEGIN · SELECT ... FOR UPDATE · UPDATE · COMMIT
    A->>R: INCR libra:ver:book:42 · INCR libra:ver:books:list · INCR libra:ver:report:popular
    A-->>C: 200
    Note over A,P: old keys with v7 are unreachable for every instance and expire by TTL<br/>the next read is a MISS with fresh data
    end
